# Line endings are normalized to LF in the repository and on checkout. Worth
# setting now, while the repository is seven files old: doing it later
# renormalizes the whole tree in one commit that touches everything and reviews
# as noise.
* text=auto eol=lf

# What a project downloads. Packagist's dist archive is `git archive`, so
# export-ignore is what keeps this package to two inert classes plus the
# notices — nothing that only matters to someone working ON the package rather
# than WITH it.
#
# LICENSE is deliberately absent from this list: MIT requires the notice to
# accompany every copy, and a Composer install is one.
/.gitattributes    export-ignore
/.gitignore        export-ignore
/.github/          export-ignore
/tests/            export-ignore
